{"parentUuid":"1b86b5fb-02f9-40c6-824d-27d18cb83cbc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KoGyptukvx9Aj2hnAiG3QS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015SdiXXP8V65jcR1MoDJCuw","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT internal LNS workers num_search_workers neighborhood types 2024 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8194,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":216,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8194},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":216,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8194,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqqBhZGuTwUsAXJApCZ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c2b6f6bf-b33b-45e7-9300-7e1e9839cfef","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:49.207Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1b86b5fb-02f9-40c6-824d-27d18cb83cbc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VBK2PNKsWezWo684V5Znis","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT large neighborhood search LNS parameters use_lns_only sat_parameters.proto\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_model_lns.h at v9.4 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.4/ortools/sat/cp_model_lns.h\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT LNS threads · Issue #1314 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1314\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at master · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.cc at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.cc\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"SatParameters in cp_sat::proto - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cp_sat/latest/cp_sat/proto/struct.SatParameters.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT's LNS (Large Neighborhood Search) parameters and the `sat_parameters.proto` file.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**`use_lns_only` Parameter:**\n\nYou can run only the incomplete subsolvers (LNS and related heuristics) by setting solver.parameters.use_lns_only = True, but this needs to be combined with a time limit, as the incomplete subsolvers do not know when to stop.\n\n**LNS in SAT Parameters:**\n\nThe `use_lns_only` parameter is an LNS parameter in SatParameters, and it works alongside other LNS-related options like `lns_focus_on_decision_variables` and `lns_expand_intervals_in_constraint_graph`.\n\n**LNS Overview:**\n\nLarge neighborhood search (LNS) is a notable strategy that tries to find a better solution by changing only a few variables.\n\nThe `sat_parameters.proto` file is located in the OR-Tools GitHub repository and contains all SAT solver parameters, including various LNS-related configuration options for controlling how the CP-SAT solver's large neighborhood search components behave during solving.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"61a9ac0a-c6df-4044-8299-1e9f7fe43996","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:54.513Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1b86b5fb-02f9-40c6-824d-27d18cb83cbc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c2b6f6bf-b33b-45e7-9300-7e1e9839cfef","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015SdiXXP8V65jcR1MoDJCuw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT internal LNS workers num_search_workers neighborhood types 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Large Neighborhood Search - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Higher num_search_workers value increases the resolution time · Issue #1921 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1921\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT LNS threads · Issue #1314 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1314\"},{\"title\":\"🎓 How the CP-SAT solver works | Just another developer\",\"url\":\"https://xiang.es/posts/explaining-cp-sat/\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding CP-SAT internal LNS workers, `num_search_workers`, and neighborhood types:\n\n## Worker Configuration\n\nWith two workers or more, CP-SAT starts using incomplete subsolvers like LNS. With five workers, CP-SAT will also have a first solution subsolver. With 32 workers, all 15 full problem subsolvers are used. For more than 32 workers, primarily the number of first solution subsolvers is increased.\n\n## LNS Neighborhood Types\n\nOnce a feasible solution is discovered, incomplete subsolvers take over, applying local search heuristics such as Large Neighborhood Search (LNS). These subsolvers attempt to improve the solution by iterating through various strategies via a Round Robin approach.\n\nThe search results show various LNS strategies being used, including: 'routing_path_lns', 'graph_arc_lns', 'graph_cst_lns', 'graph_dec_lns', 'graph_var_lns', and 'rins'.\n\n## LNS Neighborhood Selection Mechanism\n\nA copy of the model is made, and a solution is selected from the pool of solutions. A subset of variables is removed from the solution (the method for choosing this subset varies between strategies). The neighborhood of these variables is then explored for a better solution. The remaining variables are fixed to their current values in the copied model.\n\nThe search results primarily contain documentation and discussions from 2019-2024, but don't appear to contain recent 2025 updates specific to changes in these parameters.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1462afbe-69eb-470f-8e45-7937f5cbc028","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:56.773Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c2b6f6bf-b33b-45e7-9300-7e1e9839cfef","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
