{"parentUuid":"4da4c4de-f957-4bd1-a737-4e99f64ae4ef","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KCwUoCL71BJQMv6ekZEx3v","type":"tool_result","content":"# LNS Parameters and Implementation in CP-SAT\n\nBased on the provided content, here's what can be extracted:\n\n## LNS-Related Parameters\nThe document does not explicitly list CP-SAT configuration parameters like `use_lns_only` or `lns_focus_on_decision_variables`. It focuses on conceptual understanding rather than API details.\n\n## Default LNS Neighborhood Types\nCP-SAT internally employs multiple strategies, as shown in the logs:\n- `feasibility_pump`\n- `graph_arc_lns`\n- `graph_cst_lns`\n- `graph_dec_lns`\n- `graph_var_lns`\n- `rins/rens`\n- `rnd_cst_lns`\n- `rnd_var_lns`\n- `routing_path_lns`\n- `routing_random_lns`\n\nThe material notes that CP-SAT \"rates the performance of its LNS-strategies and uses the best performing strategies more often.\"\n\n## Custom LNS Implementation\nThe primer emphasizes you should write custom LNS when you have domain knowledge: \"You on the other hand know a lot about your problem and can use this knowledge to implement a more efficient version.\"\n\nCustom approaches work best when leveraging problem structure (e.g., geometric regions in TSP).\n\n## Interaction with num_search_workers\nThe document indicates that \"Whenever a worker thread finishes its work, it will execute an iteration with the next strategy in the list,\" suggesting round-robin distribution across workers.\n\n## Destroy/Repair Design\nRecommendations include:\n- Randomly select variables to reset, then optimize remaining assignments\n- Scale neighborhood size based on solver time limits\n- Use multiple neighborhood strategies with adaptive selection"}]},"uuid":"f235b44f-6fe7-41db-9602-cfde0e8f393f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:07.273Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4da4c4de-f957-4bd1-a737-4e99f64ae4ef","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1318df41-7277-4e05-b173-05fc660c5e53","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nVYGjEMrst2TRAfSiUe3v","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Parameters Search Results\n\nBased on the provided proto file content, here are the parameters matching your criteria:\n\n## LNS/Neighborhood Parameters\n\nNo parameters with \"lns\" or \"neighborhood\" explicitly in their names appear in the visible portion of the file (lines 1-1000). The file note indicates \"NEXT TAG: 356\" suggesting additional parameters exist beyond what's shown.\n\n## Hint-Related Parameters\n\n1. **use_optimization_hints** (bool, default: true)\n   - \"For an optimization problem, whether we follow some hints in order to find a better first solution.\"\n\n2. **debug_crash_on_bad_hint** (bool, default: false)\n   - \"Crash if we do not manage to complete the hint into a full solution.\"\n\n3. **debug_crash_if_presolve_breaks_hint** (bool, default: false)\n   - \"Crash if presolve breaks a feasible hint.\"\n\n4. **polarity_exploit_ls_hints** (bool, default: false)\n   - \"If true and we have first solution LS workers, tries in some phase to follow a LS solutions that violates has litle constraints as possible.\"\n\n---\n\n**Note:** The file is truncated in the provided content. Parameters like `fix_variables_to_their_hinted_value`, `repair_hint`, and LNS-specific parameters likely exist in the remainder (lines 1000+) not shown in this excerpt."}]},"uuid":"c9de7e76-0079-4373-ad9b-21afd615a6bd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:09.034Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1318df41-7277-4e05-b173-05fc660c5e53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"92a27a81-3953-4928-91d5-95d9f9d754fb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017qK162PFaF1MNsw7W5j1sN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT warm start hint solution_hint repair_hint placement problem accelerate proof optimality\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"✨ Recipes for Google OR-Tools | Just another developer\",\"url\":\"https://xiang.es/posts/cp-sat/\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the [hint] in the CP-SAT log\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/wsvOc-66-84\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPSAT presolve makes hint infeasible · Issue #4693 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4693\"},{\"title\":\"Example – IEA Wind 740-10-MW - version 0.1.2 - OptiWindNet\",\"url\":\"https://optiwindnet.readthedocs.io/v0.1.2/notebooks/04-IEA_Wind_740-10-MW_Reference_Offshore_Wind_Plants.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide you with information about CP-SAT warm start hints and related functionality:\n\n## CP-SAT Warm Start Hints Overview\n\nWarm-starting is an optimization technique where the solver uses the previous solution as a starting point or \"hint\" for the next iteration, and can significantly speed up the solving process by using the previous solution as a good starting point for repair, even if the previous solution becomes infeasible due to a newly added constraint.\n\n## Hint Mechanisms\n\n**Solution Hints:** If you have a good intuition about how the solution might look—perhaps from solving a similar model or using a good heuristic—you can inform CP-SAT to incorporate this knowledge into its search, and some workers will try to follow these hints, which can significantly improve the solver's performance if they are good.\n\n**Hint Feasibility and Pruning:** If the hints actually represent a feasible solution, the solver can use them to prune the search space of all branches that have worse bounds than the hints.\n\n## Repair Hints Parameter\n\nBecause repairing an infeasible hint can be computationally expensive, CP-SAT handles this process carefully, and you can instruct CP-SAT to attempt repairing the hint by setting solver.parameters.repair_hint = True.\n\n## Handling Incomplete Hints\n\nTo further improve this approach, you could add a heuristic to repair the hint, as a feasible hint is much more valuable than one that needs significant repair.\n\nThe search results show practical usage examples and known issues, but don't contain extensive documentation specifically about \"accelerate proof optimality\" - you may need to consult the official OR-Tools documentation for more details on proof optimality acceleration techniques with hints.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fc667646-f8dd-440a-a9a2-f4ac5dd29b63","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:13.212Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"92a27a81-3953-4928-91d5-95d9f9d754fb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
