{"parentUuid":"6d2a613d-5e70-47ce-98b0-d2bb9c8219c7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Vxt5eqaFVbkWHruNJEqZBP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018tDr2p2mU4TAT6faJ8Sd6e","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"primal heuristic dual proof exact MIP CP hybrid warm start optimality gap closing"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3008,"cache_read_input_tokens":24042,"output_tokens":262,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3008},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":262,"cache_read_input_tokens":24042,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3008,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3008,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqsH64FJC3CwcskL9ds","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"7853c294-d267-4b31-86ab-9dc88533dffc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:17.616Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"27fe059e-b562-4eaf-ac66-e7837bcb803f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VuCEGo4SW3P18DEsYmdBib","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search Pisinger Ropke 2007 destroy repair operator 2D packing placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/adaptive-large-neighborhood-search\"},{\"title\":\"A survey of adaptive large neighborhood search algorithms and applications - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054822001654\"},{\"title\":\"Large Neighborhood Search\",\"url\":\"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5293785/Pisinger.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"An adaptive large neighborhood search heuristic for Two-Echelon Vehicle Routing Problems arising in city logistics - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3587400/\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/1072464683/34\"},{\"title\":\"A review and ranking of operators in adaptive large neighborhood search for vehicle routing problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221724003928\"},{\"title\":\"An Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search Heuristic for the Pickup and Delivery Problem with Time Windows | Transportation Science\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/trsc.1050.0135\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search using the Graphics Processing Unit - SINTEF\",\"url\":\"https://www.sintef.no/en/publications/publication/1261882/\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel adaptive large neighborhood search based on spark to solve VRPTW | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-74432-2\"},{\"title\":\"Large Neighborhood Search\",\"url\":\"https://orbit.dtu.dk/files/5293785/Pisinger.pdf\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive information about Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS) by Pisinger and Ropke. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview\n\nAdaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS) was introduced by Stefan Ropke and David Pisinger, building upon the destroy-and-repair operator structure of Large Neighborhood Search (LNS) to tackle the challenge of finding global optimum solutions in complex, computationally intractable optimization problems.\n\n## Destroy and Repair Operators\n\nThe core mechanism involves the use of multiple destroy and repair operators, where a current solution is partially destroyed and subsequently repaired, enabling exploration of large neighborhoods within the solution space. More specifically, a destroy operator is first chosen to remove q customers and a repair operator is then used to insert them back into the current solution.\n\n## Adaptive Component\n\nThe adaptive aspect is achieved by recording the performance of each neighborhood operator and dynamically adjusting their selection probabilities based on their effectiveness in previous iterations, thereby enhancing search efficiency and solution quality.\n\n## Initial Development and Applications\n\nAlthough the first proposals of ALNS were devoted to transportation optimization problems, namely the Pickup and Delivery Problem with Time Windows (Ropke and Pisinger, 2006a) and the class of problems in Vehicle Routing Problems (Ropke and Pisinger, 2006b, Pisinger and Ropke, 2007, Pisinger and Ropke, 2019), numerous researchers have exhibited the tremendous effectiveness of ALNS and the flexibility of this framework has been shown in multiple domains.\n\nThe search results confirm the 2007 publication reference and document the fundamental destroy-repair operator approach, though they primarily focus on routing/transportation problems rather than 2D packing specifically.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"52ab2755-33d1-4f9b-b51b-25bbf75c2fae","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:23.288Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"27fe059e-b562-4eaf-ac66-e7837bcb803f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6d2a613d-5e70-47ce-98b0-d2bb9c8219c7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DSHZky6dnY9rH5qsbdK76r","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"reinforcement learning\" \"large neighborhood search\" 2024 2025 combinatorial optimization survey\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - RobbertReijnen/DR-ALNS: [ICAPS 2024] DR-ALNS: Deep Reinforced Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/RobbertReijnen/DR-ALNS\"},{\"title\":\"Reinforcement learning-guided adaptive large neighborhood search for vehicle routing problem with time windows | Journal of Combinatorial Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10878-025-01364-6\"},{\"title\":\"[2211.00759] Online Control of Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search using Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.00759\"},{\"title\":\"A Graph Reinforcement Learning Framework for Neural Adaptive Large Neighbourhood Search - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054824002636\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - dongjinkun/COPZoo: Neural Combinatorial Optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dongjinkun/COPZoo\"},{\"title\":\"adaptive search strategy combination algorithm based on reinforcement learning and neighborhood search | Journal of Computational Design and Engineering | Oxford Academic\",\"url\":\"https://academic.oup.com/jcde/article/12/2/177/7984516\"},{\"title\":\"RL4CO: An Extensive Reinforcement Learning for Combinatorial Optimization Benchmark | Proceedings of the 31st ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining V.2\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3711896.3737433\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"Reinforcement learning-guided adaptive large neighborhood search for vehicle routing problem with time windows | Journal of Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/s10878-025-01364-6\"},{\"title\":\"Online Control of Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search Using Deep Reinforcement Learning | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=qMo2FWCznH\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are key findings on reinforcement learning combined with large neighborhood search for combinatorial optimization in 2024-2025:\n\n## Recent Key Developments\n\n**DR-ALNS (2024):** Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) has been leveraged to configure the Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS) algorithm for solving combinatorial optimization problems. This approach outperforms vanilla ALNS, ALNS tuned with Bayesian optimization, and two state-of-the-art DRL approaches.\n\n**PPO-ALNS (2025):** A novel hybrid framework integrates Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) with Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS) for solving the Vehicle Routing Problem with Time Windows (VRPTW).\n\n**Graph-Based Approaches (2024):** Graph Reinforcement Learning for Operator Selection (GRLOS) applies Deep Reinforcement Learning and Graph Neural Networks, along with a Learned Roulette Wheel approach for operator selection in ALNS.\n\n## Broader Context\n\nALNS is a popular metaheuristic with renowned efficiency in solving combinatorial optimization problems, though the design of an effective adaptive layer for operator selection remains an open question despite 18 years of intensive research.\n\nThe field includes numerous 2024 benchmarks and surveys—a comprehensive survey on neural combinatorial optimization algorithms for vehicle routing problems was published in 2024.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"eaffa815-4818-43be-af95-9295a6c34fb3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:23.774Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6d2a613d-5e70-47ce-98b0-d2bb9c8219c7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7853c294-d267-4b31-86ab-9dc88533dffc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018tDr2p2mU4TAT6faJ8Sd6e","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"primal heuristic dual proof exact MIP CP hybrid warm start optimality gap closing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Heuristics as warm start for Mixed Integer Programming (MIP) models | Towards Data Science\",\"url\":\"https://towardsdatascience.com/heuristics-as-warm-start-for-mixed-integer-programming-mip-models-9046781dd21f/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Primal Heuristics for Mixed Integer Programs\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/258846101_Primal_Heuristics_for_Mixed_Integer_Programs\"},{\"title\":\"Measuring the impact of primal heuristics - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0167637713001181\"},{\"title\":\"CPLEX\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/latest/docs/S_CPLEX.html\"},{\"title\":\"A Hybrid Relaxation-Heuristic Framework for Solving MIP with Binary Variables\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.00429\"},{\"title\":\"Learn How NVIDIA cuOpt Accelerates Mixed Integer Optimization using Primal Heuristics | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/learn-how-nvidia-cuopt-accelerates-mixed-integer-optimization-using-primal-heuristics\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Primal Heuristics for Mixed Integer Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.20499v1\"},{\"title\":\"primal heuristics – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/tag/primal-heuristics/\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Primal Heuristics for Mixed Integer Programming\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=JtwE7RMyFR\"},{\"title\":\"What is the MIPGap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/8265539575953-What-is-the-MIPGap\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search on your query about primal heuristics, dual methods, exact MIP/CP approaches, hybrid methods, warm start techniques, and optimality gap closing. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Primal Heuristics and Solution Quality\n\nPrimal heuristics play an important role in the solving of mixed integer programs (MIPs) and often provide good feasible solutions early while helping to reduce the time needed to prove optimality. Primal heuristic methods focus on finding strong feasible solutions without a proof of optimality, and in many cases serve as one of the main tools for finding good feasible solutions when the MILP problem is too hard to solve to optimality in a given time budget.\n\n## Warm Start Approaches\n\nWarm starting the PDLP algorithm with previous primal and dual solutions from a previous projection is a technique used to improve efficiency. If a very good known solution is available and one wants to prove it is optimal or how far it is from optimal, it is not guaranteed that a MIP start, even if it is better than the solver's initial solution, will improve convergence and/or run time.\n\n## Hybrid Approaches\n\nRecent work proposes three types of relaxations to the primal problem—linear relaxation, duality relaxation, and augmented relaxation—which are further enhanced by combining them with heuristic methods to form a new, more effective approach.\n\n## Optimality Gap Closing\n\nIf incumbent is equal to the best bound, the gap is 0 and the optimal solution was found; the gap is the difference between Best Bound and Incumbent. For two state-of-the-art MIP solvers, the primal integral changes by a factor of nearly 2 when disabling primal heuristics, whereas the running time to optimality only increases moderately.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"98419415-f541-476d-87ce-cb12387fd0e6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:26.537Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7853c294-d267-4b31-86ab-9dc88533dffc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"98419415-f541-476d-87ce-cb12387fd0e6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013VWJNxouoDUocLu7zLdAfR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CyheMPMpm2Qe7EkT9zgHQW","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1314","prompt":"What does the issue say about CP-SAT LNS threads, when they activate, how they interact with num_search_workers, and any practical advice for tuning?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4537,"cache_read_input_tokens":27050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4537,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqtHKj6yAeyHMH37LVQ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"62bdc045-f27f-4d0f-9551-360e4d032abb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:29.979Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"62bdc045-f27f-4d0f-9551-360e4d032abb","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013VWJNxouoDUocLu7zLdAfR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AwgWSEAYmazMJy9aRjymzY","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750","prompt":"What is the issue about CP-SAT returning UNKNOWN with a complete solution hint? What workarounds are suggested? Specifically, what parameters help when feeding a known feasible solution as a hint?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4537,"cache_read_input_tokens":27050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4537,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqtHKj6yAeyHMH37LVQ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9362b0ee-1e8c-41bf-8228-1a2675d563ee","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:31.959Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9362b0ee-1e8c-41bf-8228-1a2675d563ee","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013VWJNxouoDUocLu7zLdAfR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YCXXu1WegCYdZnqFjhkjco","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"simulated annealing vs LNS vs genetic algorithm 2D facility placement grid feasibility comparison"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4537,"cache_read_input_tokens":27050,"output_tokens":383,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4537},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":383,"cache_read_input_tokens":27050,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4537,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4537,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqtHKj6yAeyHMH37LVQ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2b826ee8-7858-4a71-a15e-c9c9807136ec","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:32.488Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"62bdc045-f27f-4d0f-9551-360e4d032abb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CyheMPMpm2Qe7EkT9zgHQW","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT LNS Threads Issue Summary\n\nBased on the GitHub issue content provided, here's what's stated:\n\n**The Core Problem:**\nA user reported configuring the solver with `use_lns = True` and `lns_num_threads = 4`, but observed only a single thread active when monitoring processes via htop.\n\n**What the Issue Contains:**\nThe issue is primarily a question about parallelization behavior rather than a detailed explanation. The user asks \"How should the parallelization be done?\" indicating the expected multi-threaded behavior wasn't occurring as anticipated.\n\n**Notable Limitations:**\nThe provided content shows only the initial issue report itself—no responses, comments, or explanations from maintainers like lperron (the assigned developer). Therefore, the document contains:\n- No information about when LNS threads activate\n- No guidance on interaction with `num_search_workers`\n- No practical tuning advice\n\nTo find answers about LNS thread behavior and configuration best practices, you would need to review the subsequent comments, pull requests, or official documentation referenced in the actual GitHub issue thread."}]},"uuid":"0b71c83c-8a6b-4f3d-87fb-70e169830b34","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:34.959Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"62bdc045-f27f-4d0f-9551-360e4d032abb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9362b0ee-1e8c-41bf-8228-1a2675d563ee","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AwgWSEAYmazMJy9aRjymzY","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT UNKNOWN Status with Complete Solution Hint\n\n## The Issue\n\nThe user reported that CP-SAT returns an \"UNKNOWN\" status even when provided with a complete and feasible solution hint as a warm start. Specifically, when the solver stops during presolve due to a time limit, it fails to utilize the provided solution hint.\n\n## Key Problem Details\n\nThe log shows:\n- **\"The solution hint is complete and is feasible\"** - acknowledged by the solver\n- Presolve completes and stops: **\"Stopped after presolve\"**\n- Final status: **\"status: UNKNOWN\"** with objective value of 0\n\nThe solver consumed 21 seconds (exceeding the 20-second time limit) during presolve and never entered the actual search phase, meaning it couldn't leverage the hinted solution.\n\n## Suggested Workarounds\n\nWhile the content doesn't explicitly detail workarounds, the issue context suggests:\n\n1. **Increase time limits** - Allow sufficient time for presolve to complete before the wall-clock limit\n2. **Adjust presolve aggressiveness** - Consider parameters that control presolve behavior intensity\n3. **Monitor deterministic time** - The log shows deterministic_time hitting limits during probing phases\n\nThe root cause appears to be a mismatch between when presolve exhausts the time budget and the solver's inability to return the hinted solution when search never begins."}]},"uuid":"0df7f7e9-1ad1-40a1-865a-2cda8e9c1a2d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:37.415Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9362b0ee-1e8c-41bf-8228-1a2675d563ee","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2b826ee8-7858-4a71-a15e-c9c9807136ec","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YCXXu1WegCYdZnqFjhkjco","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"simulated annealing vs LNS vs genetic algorithm 2D facility placement grid feasibility comparison\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Simulated Annealing and Genetic Algorithms for the Facility Layout Problem: A Survey | Computational Optimization and Applications | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1023/A:1008623913524\"},{\"title\":\"Simulated Annealing and Genetic Algorithms for the Facility Layout Problem: A Survey | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-0-585-26778-4_7.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Hybrid Genetic-Simulated Annealing Algorithm for the Location-Inventory-Routing Problem Considering Returns under E-Supply Chain Environment - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3891439/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Simulated Annealing and Genetic Algorithms for the Facility Layout Problem: A Survey\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/226280512_Simulated_Annealing_and_Genetic_Algorithms_for_the_Facility_Layout_Problem_A_Survey\"},{\"title\":\"Simulated Annealing and Genetic Algorithms for the Facility LayoutProblem: A Survey: Computational Optimization and Applications: Vol 7, No 1\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1023/A:1008623913524\"},{\"title\":\"Simulated annealing and genetic algorithms CE 377K Stephen D. Boyles\",\"url\":\"https://sboyles.github.io/teaching/ce377k/heuristics.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Comparative Analysis between Genetic Algorithm and Simulated Annealing-Based Frameworks for Optimal Sensor Placement and Structural Health Monitoring Purposes\",\"url\":\"https://mdpi.com/2075-5309/12/9/1383/htm\"},{\"title\":\"A Hybrid Genetic Algorithm and Simulated Annealing Approach for the Uncapacitated Facility Location Problem | Computer and Decision Making: An International Journal\",\"url\":\"https://comdem.org/index.php/comdem/article/view/13781\"},{\"title\":\"Hybrid genetic algorithm and simulated annealing for two-dimensional non-guillotine rectangular packing problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0952197606000169\"},{\"title\":\"Simulated annealing and genetic algorithms for the facility layout problem: A survey\",\"url\":\"https://ftp.iaorifors.com/paper/21562\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide information about simulated annealing and genetic algorithms for facility placement problems, though the results don't contain specific details about Large Neighborhood Search (LNS). Here's what the literature shows:\n\n## Algorithm Comparison for Facility Layout/Placement\n\nThe facility layout problem (FLP) has many practical applications and is known to be NP-hard. Research has extensively compared different optimization approaches:\n\n**Simulated Annealing (SA) vs Genetic Algorithms (GA):**\nTraditional GA has strong global search ability but also has defects such as premature convergence and weak local search ability. SA, on the other hand, has strong local search ability and no premature problem. Therefore, the combination of GA and SA can overcome the defects of each of the two methods, bring into play their respective advantages, and improve the solving efficiency.\n\nGenetic algorithms maintain a larger population of solutions which reflect a diverse set of points within the feasible region, in contrast to simulated annealing where there is a single search happening through the feasible region.\n\n**Hybrid Approaches:**\nResearch shows that hybrid genetic simulated annealing algorithms outperform GA on computing time, optimal solution, and computing stability.\n\nHybrid metaheuristic algorithms integrating Genetic Algorithm and Simulated Annealing integrate the global exploration capabilities of GA with the local search effectiveness of SA to achieve robust optimization performance.\n\n**2D Packing/Placement Problems:**\nFor two-dimensional non-guillotine rectangular packing problems, genetic algorithm and simulated annealing with improved placement algorithms have been applied and compared.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about Large Neighborhood Search (LNS) comparisons for these problems. You may want to search for LNS specifically if you need that comparison.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8821df8c-901d-4746-8b63-57b4f45aa94d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:40.222Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2b826ee8-7858-4a71-a15e-c9c9807136ec","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8821df8c-901d-4746-8b63-57b4f45aa94d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a31af6debabd49128","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015HBh3p8LUu4qfKDktBN6aq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material to write the report. Let me synthesize the findings.\n\n---\n\n# LNS + Exact CP-SAT Hybrid 调研报告\n\n## 1. LNS 基础与 OR-Tools 集成\n\nLNS（Large Neighborhood Search）由 Pisinger & Røpke 提出，核心是 **destroy + repair** 算子循环：固定大部分变量，破坏一小片子集，再用某种方法修复重建。Adaptive LNS（ALNS, 2007）在此基础上多算子+权重自适应。OR-Tools 的 Routing Solver 早期就内置 LNS（`routing_path_lns` / `routing_random_lns`），CP-SAT 也在 v9 之后把 LNS 当成一线启发式使用。\n\n## 2. CP-SAT 的 LNS 参数\n\n可调参数（`sat_parameters.proto` 内）：\n\n- `use_lns_only`（bool, default false）：只跑增量启发式（LNS 等不完备求解器），不跑完备搜索。**必须配 time limit**，否则它不知道何时停。\n- `lns_focus_on_decision_variables` / `lns_expand_intervals_in_constraint_graph`：控制邻域选择。\n- `repair_hint`（bool）：当 hint 不完整或被 presolve 破坏时，让 solver 主动修复。\n- `use_optimization_hints`（默认 true）：让一部分 worker 跟随 hint 找首解。\n- `debug_crash_on_bad_hint` / `debug_crash_if_presolve_breaks_hint`：调试 hint 质量必备。\n- `polarity_exploit_ls_hints`：让全局 SAT 搜索极化方向跟随 LS（Local Search）解。\n\n详情：[sat_parameters.proto](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n\n## 3. CP-SAT 内置 LNS 邻域类型\n\n从 CP-SAT log 可见 round-robin 调度的 LNS strategies：`rnd_var_lns`、`rnd_cst_lns`、`graph_var_lns`、`graph_arc_lns`、`graph_cst_lns`、`graph_dec_lns`、`rins/rens`、`scheduling_*_lns`、`routing_path_lns`、`routing_random_lns`、`feasibility_pump`。CP-SAT 自动评估每个策略的产出并加权。\n\n## 4. num_search_workers 与 LNS 的关系\n\nCP-SAT 多 worker 架构（[CP-SAT Primer §7](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html)）：\n\n- **2+ workers**：开始引入增量 LNS subsolver。\n- **5+ workers**：加入 first-solution subsolver。\n- **32+ workers**：15 个 full-problem subsolver + 多个 LNS + first-solution 全开。\n- 超过 32 主要扩 first-solution worker。\n\n**结论**：你跑 4 worker 时 LNS 已经在跑了，但只有少量。要拿手写 LNS 加速，要么是它做的事情 CP-SAT 内置覆盖不到（领域知识强的 destroy 算子），要么是你能在 CP-SAT 之外用更便宜的启发式**先把 hint 喂进去**。\n\n## 5. ALNS 学术状态\n\n- Pisinger & Røpke 2007 综述：[Large Neighborhood Search PDF](https://orbit.dtu.dk/files/5293785/Pisinger.pdf)\n- 2024 ALNS 算子综述（VRP）：[ScienceDirect](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221724003928)\n- DR-ALNS（ICAPS 2024，Deep RL 控制 ALNS 算子选择）：[GitHub](https://github.com/RobbertReijnen/DR-ALNS)\n- Online Control of ALNS via DRL：[arXiv 2211.00759](https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.00759)\n- Graph RL Operator Selection 2024：[ScienceDirect](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054824002636)\n- 2D 非导轨矩形 packing 的 GA+SA 混合：[Sciencedirect](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0952197606000169)\n\n## 6. Hybrid: LNS warm-start + Exact 验证\n\n模式叫 **\"primal heuristic + dual proof\"**——LNS 找强 incumbent，exact solver 主要做 dual bound（剪枝 + 最优证明）。已知坑：**hint 必须能撑过 presolve**，否则 CP-SAT 会 UNKNOWN（[Issue #3750](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750)、[#4693](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4693)）。措施：\n\n1. 喂**完整 hint**（266 个设施全都赋值），不只是关键变量。\n2. 开 `repair_hint=true` 防 presolve 破坏。\n3. 开 `debug_crash_if_presolve_breaks_hint=true` 在调试期暴露问题。\n4. 喂 hint 时 incumbent 直接给 solver `AddHint()`，bound 就有了，剪枝立刻生效。\n\n## 7. LNS 的极限——硬候选 INFEASIBLE 的事实\n\n**关键**：LNS 是 primal 启发式，**只能找 feasible 解**。对 UNSAT 问题 LNS 完全无效——它跑到死也输出不了 infeasibility certificate。你 8 个硬候选大概率 UNSAT（master CP-SAT 4 分钟超时本身已经是强暗示），LNS 在这些候选上**省不了一秒**。Dual proof（infeasibility）只能靠 exact 完备搜索 + cut/learnt clause/bound propagation，没有捷径。\n\n## 8. 70×70 placement 的具体方案\n\n**Destroy 算子（领域驱动）**：\n\n- **Spatial window destroy**：随机选 15×15 窗口，移除窗口内全部设施（重排局部 packing）。\n- **Type destroy**：移除某一类设施（如所有 power pole），让 repair 重新找位置。\n- **Worst-fit destroy**：移除占用 area 最低的 5% 设施。\n- **Binding-conflict destroy**：根据 binding subproblem 失败原因，移除涉及未满足端口的设施。\n\n**Repair 算子**：\n\n- **Greedy bottom-left fill**：按 area desc 排序，bottom-left 最先合法位置。\n- **Mini CP-SAT solve**：固定其余设施，对 destroy 出来的 sub-region 跑 5 秒 CP-SAT。这是 OR-Tools 官方推荐的 LNS repair 方式。\n- **Sequential placement + backtrack**：贪心放，冲突时回退。\n\n**与 exact 衔接**：\n\n```python\n# 伪代码\nincumbent = run_alns(time_budget=60s)  # 找 feasible\nfor var, val in incumbent.items():\n    model.AddHint(var, val)\nsolver.parameters.repair_hint = True\nsolver.parameters.use_optimization_hints = True\nsolver.parameters.num_search_workers = 8\nstatus = solver.Solve(model)  # exact verify\n```\n\n**预期收益**：\n\n- 对 **FEASIBLE 软候选**：从 4 分钟 master 超时 → 30 秒-2 分钟（incumbent 直接给 dual bound 强剪枝）。**乐观估计 5-10x 加速**。\n- 对 **INFEASIBLE 硬候选**：**0% 加速**。LNS 跑 60 秒输出 \"no feasible found\"，然后 exact 还是要原本 4 分钟。**净增 60 秒开销**。\n- 折中：**只在被分类为可能 FEASIBLE 的候选上跑 LNS 预热**。可以用你 S4 AI 数据集的 feature classifier 判定候选 promise，promise > 阈值才跑 LNS。\n\n## 9. 替代方法对比\n\n| 方法 | 找 feasible 速度 | 实现成本 | 对硬候选 | 推荐度 |\n|------|----------------|---------|---------|-------|\n| **Greedy + 修正** | 快（秒级） | 低 | 无效 | 高，作为 LNS initial |\n| **ALNS** | 中（分钟级） | 中 | 无效 | 中，需要写 4-6 个算子 |\n| **Simulated Annealing** | 中 | 低 | 无效 | 低，邻域比 LNS 小，placement 收敛慢 |\n| **Genetic Algorithm** | 慢 | 高 | 无效 | 低，266 设施编码爆炸 |\n| **CP-SAT `use_lns_only=true`** | 快 | 极低 | 无效 | 高，零代码 |\n\n## 10. 落地建议\n\n**第 1 步（零成本，1 天）**：\n直接试 `use_lns_only=true` + `num_search_workers=8` + 60s 预热，把找到的 incumbent 作为 hint 喂回完备 CP-SAT。这一步不写一行 LNS 代码，直接验证 hybrid 是否对你 problem 有效。\n\n**第 2 步（有效则深化，1 周）**：\n写 spatial window + type destroy + greedy bottom-left repair，跑 ALNS 60-120 秒。Python 的 [`alns`](https://pypi.org/project/alns/) 库可以直接用，不用从零写框架。\n\n**第 3 步（仅 FEASIBLE 候选）**：\n用 S4 AI classifier 标记候选 promise，只在 promise > 0.5 的候选上跑 LNS 预热。硬候选 / UNSAT 候选直接走原 exact 路径，省时间。\n\n**红线（按 CLAUDE.md AI Safety Contract）**：LNS 输出**只能作为 hint**，不能作为 proof source；不能写 `data/checkpoints/`；不能影响 final preflight；UNSAT 判定永远归 exact CP-SAT。\n\n---\n\n## Sources\n\n- [sat_parameters.proto (stable)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [CP-SAT Primer §5 Parameters](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer §6 Coding Patterns](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer §7 Under the Hood](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer §9 Large Neighborhood Search](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html)\n- [or-tools Issue #1314 LNS threads](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1314)\n- [or-tools Issue #3750 UNKNOWN with feasible hint](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750)\n- [or-tools Issue #4693 Presolve breaks hint](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4693)\n- [Pisinger & Røpke - Large Neighborhood Search PDF](https://orbit.dtu.dk/files/5293785/Pisinger.pdf)\n- [ALNS survey 2022 (Computers & OR)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054822001654)\n- [ALNS operator review 2024 (EJOR)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221724003928)\n- [DR-ALNS (ICAPS 2024)](https://github.com/RobbertReijnen/DR-ALNS)\n- [Online Control of ALNS via DRL (arXiv 2211.00759)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.00759)\n- [Graph RL Operator Selection for ALNS 2024](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054824002636)\n- [GA+SA hybrid for 2D non-guillotine packing](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0952197606000169)\n- [Heuristics as warm start for MIP](https://towardsdatascience.com/heuristics-as-warm-start-for-mixed-integer-programming-mip-models-9046781dd21f/)\n- [Primal Heuristics for MIPs](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/258846101_Primal_Heuristics_for_Mixed_Integer_Programs)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2879,"cache_read_input_tokens":31587,"output_tokens":4407,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2879},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4407,"cache_read_input_tokens":31587,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2879,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2879,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoquGX8fGoFEju4BAb2X","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd2f31cf-c60b-4c91-b42a-6701431b3656","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:49.117Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
